## Why This Is Asked
Tests solving interdependent CV tasks under tight latency with on-device adaptation for unseen objects, in realistic cluttered scenes.

## Key Concepts
- Shared backbone with multi-head decoders
- Joint losses: depth, normals, affordance, temporal consistency
- 5-shot on-device adaptation for novel objects
- Edge-GPU constraints (<25 ms) and robustness to occlusion/dynamic lighting

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-architecture wiring
function forward(x) {
  const z = encoder(x);
  const d = depthHead(z);
  const n = normalsHead(z);
  const a = affordanceHead(z);
  return { depth: d, normals: n, affordances: a };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you diagnose a failing grasp affordance map with occlusion?
- What ablations would you run to validate the importance of temporal consistency?

## Why This Is Asked
This angle tests end-to-end 3D understanding of dense retail shelves and edge adaptation for unseen products.

## Key Concepts
- Monocular 6-DoF pose with template-based fit
- Synthetic+real data strategy for crowded shelves
- On-device 5-shot adaptation with lightweight adapters
- Occlusion-aware pose and neighbor interaction modeling

## Code Example
```javascript
function forward(input) {
  const features = backbone(input);
  const detections = detectorHead(features);
  const poses = poseHead(features, detections);
  return {detections, poses};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How do you handle multiple identical items and permutation ambiguity?
- How would you evaluate robustness to lighting and glare on glossy shelves?

## Why This Is Asked
